/-! # Filtered cohomology colimits for finite cofinal covering families

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology on Sites, Tag 0739,
`lemma-colim-works-over-collection`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-site-finite-cover-cohomology-colimit).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace CategoryTheory.Sheaf

/-- Cohomology over the objects of `B` commutes with filtered colimits when a cofinal
collection of finite coverings has all its positive-length iterated overlaps in `B`.
`S` records actual choices of those fibre products and their universal properties.
It imposes no existence of unrelated products or of a terminal object of the site.

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology on Sites, Tag 0739,
`lemma-colim-works-over-collection`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-site-finite-cover-cohomology-colimit).

Proof, following the node's four steps:
1. Finite cofinal refinements make every object of `B` quasi-compact. The pairwise
   overlaps of selected covers lie in `B`, so are quasi-compact too. Apply
   lem-sfb-site-quasi-compact-section-colimit to get the canonical section comparison
   on `B`. The identification of degree-zero cohomology with sections in
   def-weil-pbc-sites-and-cohomology proves the degree-zero case.
2. For a filtered diagram of injectives, finite products commute with its colimit by
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimits-commute-finite-limits. Step 1 on every iterated overlap
   identifies the Cech cochains of the colimit with the colimits of the stage cochains
   from def-weil-pbc-site-cech-complex. Naturality of each coprojection commutes with
   each alternating restriction and hence with the differential. The stage Cech
   complexes are acyclic in positive degrees by lem-weil-pbc-site-injective-cech-acyclic.
   Exactness of filtered abelian-group colimits, from
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-abelian-groups-exact, gives positive Cech vanishing for
   their colimit. Empty covers have zero cochains and cause no exception.
3. Apply lem-weil-pbc-site-cech-vanishing-criterion with the given cofinality and
   overlap hypotheses. The colimit of any injective diagram is acyclic on every
   object of `B`; injectivity of the colimit itself is not asserted.
4. Abelian sheaves form a Grothendieck abelian category by
   lem-cbc-sieve-module-sheaves-grothendieck at the integers. The covering and generated
   sieve descriptions agree by lem-trf-generated-precoverage-sheaf-criterion:
   pullbacks of generated covering sieves are generated by the covering pullbacks,
   and their unique amalgamation condition is the covering equalizer condition.
   Evaluation is additive and left exact by def-weil-pbc-sites-and-cohomology.
   Filtered colimits are exact in sheaves by
   lem-weil-pbc-site-abelian-sheaves-filtered-colimits-exact and in abelian groups by
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-abelian-groups-exact. Induct on the degree using
   lem-weil-pbc-right-derived-filtered-colimit-successor, with step 1 as the base
   and step 3 supplying acyclicity. The comparison is induced by applying cohomology
   to the colimit coprojections, exactly `colimit.post` below. -/
theorem isIso_cohomology_colimit_of_finite_covers
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : Precoverage C)
    (hJ : J.IsSiteForCoverings)
    [HasSheafify J.toGrothendieck AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf J.toGrothendieck AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
    (B : Set C)
    (Cov : ∀ (V : C) (T : Type u) (W : T → C), (∀ t, W t ⟶ V) → Prop)
    (S : ∀ (V : C) (T : Type u) (W : T → C) (f : ∀ t, W t ⟶ V),
      Cov V T W f → SiteCechComplex W f)
    (hcover : ∀ (V : C) (T : Type u) (W : T → C) (f : ∀ t, W t ⟶ V),
      Cov V T W f → Presieve.ofArrows W f ∈ J V)
    (hfinite : ∀ (V : C) (T : Type u) (W : T → C) (f : ∀ t, W t ⟶ V),
      Cov V T W f → Finite T)
    (hB : ∀ (V : C) (T : Type u) (W : T → C) (f : ∀ t, W t ⟶ V)
      (h : Cov V T W f), V ∈ B ∧ (∀ t, W t ∈ B) ∧
        ∀ (p : ℕ) (a : Fin (p + 1) → T), (S V T W f h).W p a ∈ B)
    (hcofinal : ∀ (V : C), V ∈ B →
      ∀ (T : Type u) (W : T → C) (f : ∀ t, W t ⟶ V),
        Presieve.ofArrows W f ∈ J V →
        ∃ (K : Type u) (Z : K → C) (g : ∀ k, Z k ⟶ V),
          Cov V K Z g ∧ ∀ k, ∃ (t : T) (a : Z k ⟶ W t), a ≫ f t = g k)
    (D : Type u) [SmallCategory D] [IsFiltered D]
    (F : D ⥤ Sheaf J.toGrothendieck AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (U : C) (hU : U ∈ B) (q : ℕ) :
    IsIso (colimit.post F
      (cohomologyPresheafFunctor J.toGrothendieck q ⋙
        (evaluation Cᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (op U))) := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory.Sheaf
